  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Emergency Shelter Non-Food Items (NFI&apos;s) to Communities in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Ethiopia, the internal displacement, and humanitarian needs primarily stem from a combination of drivers including armed conflicts occurring in various regions, severe droughts, and floods across the country. These ongoing conflicts, climate-related shocks, and displacements present significant protection challenges for the affected population. Most displaced individuals reside in collective sites or spontaneous settlements, where they face limited access to vital services, inadequate living conditions, and a lack of necessary resources to support their families and communities. 
 
IOM, backed by ShelterBox and in partnership with the Shelter and Non-Food Item (SNFI) Cluster, aims to aid 7,000 households (38,500 individuals) in enhancing their living conditions through the provision of emergency shelter (ES)/NFIs assistance. The main target areas for this response, as identified by the cluster, include Tigray, Amhara, SNNPR, Afar, Gambella, Benishangul-Gumuz, Oromia, and Somali regions.</narrative>
  </description>
